cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CRPTO research code and reproducibility package"
message: >
  If you use this software, cite the repository and the current manuscript.
  Source code is MIT-licensed; narrative content, figures, tables, and
  documentation identified in LICENSE-CONTENT are CC BY 4.0.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Carlos Alfredo
    family-names: Vergara Rojas
    email: cavr94@gmail.com
abstract: >
  Reproducible code, protocols, tests, and aggregate evidence for an exact
  geometric analysis and identification audit of binary conformal prediction
  sets at the interface with credit portfolio optimization. The active
  manuscript reports the exact threshold characterization, complete
  finite-archive bounds, and comparator-support diagnostics without selecting a
  learner, conformal recipe, ruler, coordinate, or portfolio policy.
keywords:
  - credit risk
  - conformal prediction
  - predict-then-optimize
  - portfolio optimization
  - partial identification
  - reproducibility
license: MIT
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-07-21"
url: "https://github.com/EigenCharlie/Paper_CRPTO"
repository-code: "https://github.com/EigenCharlie/Paper_CRPTO"
